    },
    {
      "_type": "UMLActivity",
      "_id": "865997849d8f432391731d6f3ec2caf5",
      "_parent": {
        "$ref": "33c8f96b77c54940b1450d20afa8784b"
      },
      "name": "AD-03 - Medicine Matching & Pharmacist Verification",
      "visibility": "public",
      "isAbstract": false,
      "isReadOnly": false,
      "isSingleExecution": false,
      "documentation": "Activity Diagram derived from UC-07 (Medicine Matching), UC-08 (Request Pharmacist Verification), UC-09 (Pharmacist Reviews Comparison), UC-10 (Pharmacist Verifies Comparison), and UC-11 (User Receives Verified Comparison).\n\nShows the workflow through which a user selects a medicine/product for comparison, MedAccess identifies a potential matching product using structured medicine attributes (active ingredient, strength, dosage form, pack size, manufacturer where applicable), and \u2014 if the user requests it \u2014 an authorized pharmacist reviews and verifies or rejects the proposed comparison before any result is presented as verified.\n\nCentral safety principle: the system may identify a potential matching product, but it must not independently authorize medicine substitution. A structured match is an informational result only. Pharmacist verification is required before a comparison is treated as verified; if pharmacist review is unavailable the comparison remains pending and is never shown as verified; if the pharmacist rejects the comparison it is never shown as verified.\n\nPreconditions:\n1. The user can access the medicine comparison function (authentication is treated as a precondition, not part of this workflow).\n2. The MedAccess medicine catalogue and structured medicine attributes are potentially accessible.\n3. A pharmacist account with verification authority may or may not be available at review time.\n\nPostconditions (success - verified): the pharmacist has confirmed the comparison; the verification, reviewer identity, and timestamp are recorded; the comparison status is set to verified; the user is shown the verified result.\nPostconditions (rejected): the pharmacist has rejected the comparison; the decision is recorded; the comparison status is set to not verified; the user is shown the non-verified result.\nPostconditions (pending): pharmacist review was not available; the comparison remains pending and is never presented as verified.\nPostconditions (no result): matching information was insufficient, OR no matching product was found, OR the user chose not to request verification of an informational match.\n\nOut of scope: diagnosis, prescription generation, automatic prescribing, automatic medicine substitution, dosage or treatment recommendations, automatic clinical equivalence decisions, purchase, payment, delivery, dispensing, controlled/narcotic/psychotropic/high-risk medicine workflows, and any implementation-level database/API detail. Price is never treated as a matching criterion.\n\nTraceability: UC-07 - Medicine Matching; UC-08 - Request Pharmacist Verification; UC-09 - Pharmacist Reviews Comparison; UC-10 - Pharmacist Verifies Comparison; UC-11 - User Receives Verified Comparison.",
      "ownedElements": [
